            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>To be accurate with chronic pain assessment, the medical examiner should be alert to specific diagnoses in addition to global markers of decreased function associated with chronic pain, such as disability and depression. The key to accurate assessment is to avoid making assumptions before doing a complete history and physical examination. This article focuses on the history and examination and emphasizes pitfalls associated with overreliance on medical technology.</AbstractText>
